# Game scene / match

## Ownership

- Orchestration: `game.gd` applies `GameConfig` via `ResourceUtils.update_resource`
- Rules + physics: `VolleySim` only (`src/features/volley_sim/`) — see `simulation.mdc`
- Scene side: `MatchRunner` feeds the sim, `MatchView` draws it; views are `blob_view` / `ball_view`

## Change guide

| Goal | Touch |
|------|--------|
| Round / match transitions, scoring, 3-touch fault, timer | `VolleySim` (+ test in `tests/cases/test_volley_sim.gd`) |
| Player / ball feel (speeds, bounce, hit) | constants in `VolleySim` |
| Visuals, HUD text, FX | `MatchView`, `BlobView`, `BallView` |
| Bot | `src/features/ai_opponent/` |
| Input mapping | `src/features/player_input/`, `project.godot` InputMap (P1 device 0 / P2 device 1) |
| Touch / virtual stick | `src/features/virtual_controls/` — analog left-half drag, right half jump; right-mid **BOOM** only if touchscreen |
| Online | `src/features/online/online_rollback.gd` (`online.md`) |

## Constraints

- Exit match via `root_events.ev_exit_game` with post-battle payload (from `MatchRunner.ev_match_over`)
- `vs_ai` / `max_touches` / `online` / `ranked` / `local_side` come from `GameConfig`, not hardcoded
- Never put gameplay rules in `game.gd`, views or the AI; never read engine physics for gameplay
- More than `max_touches` (default 3) on one side → fault, opponent scores
- No dual-touch local 2P: both halves are **P1 only**; P2 uses keyboard / pad1 (`p2_*`)
- Online 1v1: every peer runs the full sim; only inputs are exchanged (rollback); host = left/Blue
- Last-chance blast: once per round; offline Blue only, online both sides; BOOM UI mirrors `VolleySim.can_blast`
